        "display": "All five tests passed with exit code 0. Ordinary CODER handoff follows.\n\n## Handoff — CODER (subtask `lru`)\n\n**Work performed**\n- Read the existing files first: `lru-cache.cjs` was a stub (`// Fixed incomplete LRU fixture. module.exports = {};`), and `lru-cache.test.cjs` contained the five required tests.\n- Implemented `lru-cache.cjs` as CommonJS exporting `LRUCache` (applied via `workspace_apply` with the original expected version/readReceiptId):\n  - `constructor(capacity, ttlMs = Infinity)` — validates a positive integer capacity.\n  - `get(key)` — returns the value or `undefined`; expired entries (TTL elapsed since last `set`) are removed and yield `undefined`; live entries are deleted/reinserted to refresh recency.\n  - `set(key, value)` — inserts/updates, refreshing recency, records an `expiresAt` from the last set time, and evicts the least-recently-used entry while capacity is exceeded.\n  - `delete(key)` — returns whether the key existed (`Map.delete` semantics).\n- `lru-cache.test.cjs` preserved byte-for-byte unchanged (sha256 `0336e968…` matches baseline).\n\n**Test evidence**\n- Command: `node --test --test-reporter=tap @input/lru-cache.test.cjs`\n- Input version: `manifest:5a59d34d958dfd339cd0972ddca195f2a6cee3a74e14c84f269f3ef462b252d0` (manifestHash `5a59d34d…`), captured via `workspace_read` with no path after the apply.\n- Receipt: `run:ad4e2f1f3169b9d72d19a360a1d8f4d92c7cd16cf9b9a018ab113b97fc58b4d5`, `exitCode: 0`, no timeout, no stderr.\n- TAP result: `1..5`, `# tests 5`, `# pass 5`, `# fail 0` — all five subtests `ok`:\n  1. missing keys return undefined\n  2. get refreshes recency and capacity evicts oldest\n  3. updating a key preserves capacity\n  4. delete removes only the chosen key\n  5. optional TTL expires entries\n- No tests were modified or skipped; no fabricated receipts.\n\n**File references**\n- `lru-cache.cjs` — now sha256 `f044cdcb618707091e54040a02fa50575415c2f97eadc17a6abfce4f53a26f13`, size 1129.\n- `l